{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vfd4N8CtEo2NtJdFMFpet9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-548\"\n3\ttitle = \"Stall guard: a reviewer outage never closes a lane partial (the 2026-08-30 plan's C1-C7)\"\n4\tspecref = \"\"\n5\tworkstream = \"process\"\n6\tsr_refs = []\n7\tneeds = []\n8\tbuildtier = \"strong\"\n9\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n10\tpriority = 1\n11\t+++\n12\t\n13\t## Deliverable\n14\t\n15\tThe seven stall-guard changes (C1-C7 of\n16\t`docs/plans/2026-08-30-stall-guard-plan.md`), built by hand on this claim\n17\tbranch under the tracked pause and verified by tests AND on a bootstrapped\n18\tscaffold:\n19\t\n20\t- **C1** `agent_loop.RoutingState` splits the builder's stall streak from\n21\t  review-draw failures (`note_session(judging=)`, `note_review_draw_failure`,\n22\t  reset on any recorded verdict) — three reviewer outages are no longer the\n23\t  builder \"not building\".\n24\t- **C2** `EXIT_REVIEW_OWED = 9`: a committed build whose review ladder is\n25\t  exhausted parks the lane (banner + `out/review-owed` marker); the\n26\t  dispatcher resumes it like a crash, the resumed worker schedules the owed\n27\t  round FIRST, a completed round clears the marker. Never a `partial` close\n28\t  of finished work.\n29\t- **C3** `agent_session.run_session(idle_timeout=)`: a silent child is killed\n30\t  ~`idle_timeout` s after its last output line (engine default 900;\n31\t  `AGENT_SESSION_IDLE_TIMEOUT` slot in all four launchers,\n32\t  `--session-idle-timeout`, forwarded by `lane.worker_argv`; typed\n33\t  `timeout: wall|idle` telemetry key).\n34\t- **C4** `probe_route`/`select_with_probe`: a route cooled earlier this run\n35\t  answers a 30 s `OK` probe on its own CmdTemplate (verbatim) before another\n36\t  real session is spent on it; clean routes are never probed.\n37\t- **C5** the same-family reviewer fallback rung: exhausted cross-family\n38\t  ladder -> relaxed retry; ANY same-family review draw is recorded three ways\n39\t  (`-relaxed` verdict filename, `heterogeneity=relaxed` round line, typed\n40\t  telemetry key).\n41\t- **C6** the close rituals in `worker.template.md` and\n42\t  `adjudicate-disposition.template.md` (the adjudicator closes its OWN row;\n43\t  draft shape pinned: this spec's `## Dispositions`, top-level keys, title\n44\t  <= 120), and `integrate` unload sheds the loop's own `out/run-logs/`\n45\t  streams + the `out/review-owed` marker as declared residue (two shipped\n46\t  pins deliberately overturned, the overturn stated in the rewritten tests).\n47\t- **C7** the reviewer brief's reading scope: exact three-dot diff against the\n48\t  CURRENT trunk with telemetry/record/generated exclusions, summary-only\n49\t  harness reads, cited-rows-only registry reads, and `{trunk}` /\n50\t  `{process_doc}` as loop-rendered slots (`trunk_name`, `process_doc_path`) —\n51\t  proven both ways: the meta-repo renders `project-trajectory/PROCESS.md`,\n52\t  the bootstrapped scaffold renders `docs/process.md`. The TERRA row carries\n53\t  `-c model_reasoning_effort=medium` as the measured item-5 experiment.\n54\t\n55\tAdopter compatibility per the plan's §6: exit 9 appended at the end of the\n56\talphabet and documented in PROCESS_OPTIONS.md \"Unattended operation\"; the\n57\tlauncher slot landed in template + live launchers in the same commit\n58\t(test_dogfood_sync parity); RESYNC_PACK.md carries this change set's entry\n59\tPLUS the two entries the previous run owed (the check_docs HTML-comment fix,\n60\topencode `--dir .`).\n61\t\n62\tVerification: full suite 3175 passed, 16 skipped in 861.84s (fig: cmd=\"python -m pytest -q -n auto\" on the lane at 777bbbfe, loaded box); guard suites 107 + 121 passed; scaffold drive: bootstrap from this branch's kit ->\n63\tone managed `--wi` session end to end (build + review), the brief rendering\n64\tthe scaffold-side slot values. Module-size ratchet re-stamped with reasons\n65\t(agent_loop 3622 -> 3924, agent_common 2660 -> 2678, integrate 2626 -> 2646).\n66\t\n67\t## Context\n68\t\n69\tThe plan of record is `docs/plans/2026-08-30-stall-guard-plan.md`, written at\n70\tthe owner's request after the 2026-08-30 unattended run (its evidence rows:\n71\tdecisions 14, 17, 21, 23, 29, 30 of `docs/decisions-for-review-2026-08-31.md`).\n72\tThe owner's direction: *\"If both openai and opencode are unavailable, I would\n73\texpect the fallback to be an independent opus reviewer, not a partial WI\"* —\n74\tand these changes land FIRST, by hand on a claim branch, before the frontier\n75\tunpauses (the tracked `docs/work/pause` holds it).\n76\t\n77\tScope is the plan's C1-C7, one row (the plan's §3 offered one or two rows;\n78\tfolded into one so the pause lifts after a single reviewed merge):\n79\t\n80\t- C1 route-aware stall accounting (`agent_loop.RoutingState` splits the build\n81\t  stall from review draw failures).\n82\t- C2 \"review owed\" as a parked state (`EXIT_REVIEW_OWED`, not a decided\n83\t  handback; persisted so a resumed worker schedules the round).\n84\t- C3 an idle deadline in `agent_session.run_session` (launcher/env slot,\n85\t  dogfood-sync parity on the launchers).\n86\t- C4 a pre-dispatch liveness probe on routes with an unclean history this run.\n87\t- C5 the same-family reviewer fallback rung, `heterogeneity=relaxed` recorded\n88\t  on the verdict path, the round line and the telemetry.\n89\t- C6 the worker/adjudicator close ritual in the shipped briefs, and\n90\t  `integrate.unload` shedding the loop's own `out/run-logs/` streams.\n91\t- C7 the review brief's reading scope (three-dot diff against the current\n92\t  trunk with telemetry/generated exclusions, summary-not-transcript harness\n93\t  reads, cited registry rows only, `{trunk}`/`{process_doc}` rendered as slots\n94\t  because this meta-repo has no `docs/process.md` while every adopter does).\n95\t\n96\tAdopter compatibility is the plan's §6: the new exit code lands at the END of\n97\tthe alphabet w